  "notes": [
    "functions: flutter test collects no function coverage (flutter_tools test/coverage_collector.dart never passes functionCoverage to package:coverage), so lcov.info has no FN/FNDA records. They are derived the way package:coverage derives them, and on 2026-09-24 matched a real package:coverage run with function coverage on (the same functions, 192 at the time, and the same 4 misses; the total grows with the code, so read it from totals.functions). The functions are the named, non-abstract, non-external declarations of each file (top-level functions, getters and setters; methods, getters, setters, operators and constructors of classes, mixins, enums and extensions) plus the constructor the compiler adds to an enum that declares none, which the VM lists; closures and local functions are not counted, as in package:coverage. A function counts as covered when lcov.info has a hit on the line where its declaration starts (its first annotation, else its first token): the line the Dart VM records the function entry on. perFile.missedFunctions lists the misses. Enum constructors never run (enum values are constants), so they are always misses.",
    "complete is false when a file in that scope is missing from lcov.info; its pct values are then null, and covered/total count measured files only.",
    "regions is null: Dart coverage has no region data.",
    "branches come from Dart VM branch coverage (BRDA). A branch counts as covered when its taken count is above 0.",
    "JavaScript inside Dart string literals (lib/src/widget_html.dart page builders) counts as covered once the Dart builder runs; its runtime behavior is not measured here.",
    "Lines under // coverage:ignore-* comments are dropped by flutter test before lcov.info is written; every such comment is listed in ignoredLines. An ignore-line or ignore-start must name its A10 category in its reason, and an ignore-file needs its file in excluded."
